# Reference for spec_library/block_model/named_objects.feature (GitHub issue
# #179): object_delete drops a named object, after which reading one of its
# properties gives unit again. zs_explore's breadth-first search creates a named
# Dict for its visited set and deletes it on the way out.

make a function called start returns r
  new("Dict", "scratch_set")
  send("scratch_set", "set", "k", 1)
  print(get("scratch_set", "k"))
  print(object_delete("scratch_set"))
  print(type_of(get("scratch_set", "k")))
end

start()
